    {
      "id": 39,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -680,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        1300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 38,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.1 [dev]: text-to-image, ControlNet, Hires. fix\n\nThe FLUX.1 [dev] workflow with every Generate and ControlNet tab feature that ComfyUI offers for it. Write full\ndescriptive sentences and put literal text in quotes; there is no negative prompt (embedded guidance, not true CFG).\n\n**Settings**: 20 steps (28-30 for finals), guidance 3.5 (Distilled CFG in the Generate tab), euler, simple,\n1024×1024 or another ~1 MP size (multiples of 16). **Width** and **Height** feed the latent and **ModelSamplingFlux**,\nwhose shift grows with the image size.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate / ControlNet tab |\n|--------|------|---------------------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed (RandomNoise), steps and scheduler (BasicScheduler), sampling method, Distilled CFG (FluxGuidance), size (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:smp:1` | Hires. fix sampler | Hires. fix: upscaler (Hires. fix upscaler), scale (Hires. fix scale), steps and denoising (Hires. fix scheduler) |\n| `ib:hr` | Hires. fix (If/Else Switch) | Hires. fix checkbox; switched on by the Upscale button |\n| `ib:cn:0` | ControlNet Depth | ControlNet tab, unit 1 |\n| `ib:cn:1` | ControlNet Canny | ControlNet tab, unit 2 |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**ControlNet** ([Union Pro 2.0](https://huggingface.co/Shakker-Labs/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0): canny, soft\nedge, depth, pose, gray in one model, no control type to set): each unit is an **Apply ControlNet** node, bypassed\nwhile the unit is disabled; Enable in the ControlNet tab turns it on. The tab sets weight (strength) and guidance range,\nthe model, the control image (**Send to ControlNet**, a drop, or Photoshop: *ControlNet: preprocess* runs the\npreprocessor and sends the map back) and the preprocessor of its **AIO Aux Preprocessor** (Depth Anything V2 and\nCanny here; set it to *none* for a ready-made map). The model card's settings: canny 0.7 / end 0.8, soft edge\n(AnylineDetector) 0.7 / 0.8, depth 0.8 / 0.8, pose (DWPose) 0.9 / 0.65, gray 0.9 / 0.8. An end of 0.6-0.8 avoids\nplastic skin and baked-in edge lines before the strength needs lowering. Both units can run together (one model\nfile, loaded once). FLUX has no negative conditioning; **Negative for the ControlNet nodes** only fills their\nnegative input. The core apply node has no mask input, so Use Mask is not offered.\n\n**Hires. fix** upscales the first pass to *Upscale by* (1.5×), encodes it again and samples it with its own\n**Hires. fix scheduler** (shift for the new size): *Hires steps* are the steps that run, at the end of a schedule of\nsteps / denoising (12 steps at 0.4). It shares noise, guider (and so the ControlNet) and sampler with the first pass.\n\n**Upscaler**: **Hires. fix upscaler** (`Load Upscale Model`, the Upscaler list of the Generate tab)\nenlarges the first pass by its own factor, and **Resize to the hires size** brings it to the first pass size ×\n*Upscale by* (**Hires. fix scale** only computes that size). Put any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here). The loader must name an installed model\neven while Hires. fix is off, since ComfyUI checks every node before running.\n\n**Hires. fix ib:hr** (`If/Else Switch`) is the Hires. fix checkbox of the Generate tab: on, it saves the\nHires. fix image; off, the first pass image, and the Hires. fix nodes do not run (its inputs are lazy). The\n**Upscale** button of the image lists switches it on, generates the image again with its seed and parameters, and\nswitches it back, so drafts made with Hires. fix off can be upscaled later (keep the size the same).\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt.\n\nBatch generation, model and LoRA exploration, varying parameters, PNG Info, projects and the Compare tab work\nas with every marked workflow. There is no reference slot: image references need FLUX.1 Kontext [dev] or Redux.\n\n## Required custom nodes\n\n- **comfyui_controlnet_aux** for the preprocessors (without it, set the preprocessors to *none* or delete them and\n  link the control images to the apply nodes).\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux1-dev-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Kijai/flux-fp8/resolve/main/flux1-dev-fp8.safetensors) (Kijai, fp8 e4m3fn, 12 GB;\nthe bf16 [flux1-dev.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-dev) of Black Forest Labs is gated)\n**text_encoders**: [clip_l.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/clip_l.safetensors),\n[t5xxl_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp16.safetensors)\n(or [t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors) with less memory)\n**vae**: [ae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Lumina_Image_2.0_Repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/vae/ae.safetensors)\n**controlnet**: [FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/ABDALLALSWAITI/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0-fp8/resolve/main/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors)\n(saved as `diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors`: rename it; 2 GB, the bf16 original of\n[Shakker-Labs](https://huggingface.co/Shakker-Labs/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0) has 4 GB)\n\nFLUX.1 [dev] is under the FLUX.1 [dev] non-commercial license.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.1 [dev] (Image Bench, all features)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
